@startuml cls-identity-authorization
title Class Diagram — Identity & Authorization

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho
hide circle

enum AuthenticationType <<enumeration>> {
  Local
  Windows
  External
}

enum SessionStatus <<enumeration>> {
  Active
  Closed
}

class Credentials <<value object>> {
  +identifier: String
  +password: String
}

class Person {
  +personId: UUID
  +documentType: String
  +documentNumber: String
  +name: String
  +lastName: String
  +email: String
  +phone: String
  +bloodType: String
  +birthDate: Date
  +status: Boolean
  +activate()
  +deactivate()
}

class AppUser {
  +userId: UUID
  +personId: UUID
  +username: String
  +passwordHash: String
  +authenticationType: AuthenticationType
  +status: Boolean
  +lastAccess: DateTime
  +authenticate(credentials: Credentials): UserSession
  +activate()
  +deactivate()
}

class UserSession {
  +sessionId: UUID
  +userId: UUID
  +startDate: DateTime
  +endDate: DateTime
  +sourceIp: String
  +sessionStatus: SessionStatus
  +close()
  +refresh(): UserSession
}

class PasswordPolicy {
  +policyId: Int
  +minLength: Int
  +maxLength: Int
  +requiresUppercase: Boolean
  +requiresNumbers: Boolean
  +requiresSymbols: Boolean
  +expirationDays: Int
}

class Role {
  +roleId: Int
  +roleName: String
  +description: String
}

class Permission {
  +permissionId: Int
  +permissionName: String
  +description: String
}

class RolePermission {
  +roleId: Int
  +permissionId: Int
  +assignmentDate: DateTime
}

class UserRole {
  +userId: UUID
  +roleId: Int
  +assignmentDate: DateTime
}

Person "1" -- "0..1" AppUser : app_user.person_id FK\nUNIQUE
AppUser "1" -- "0..*" UserSession : user_session.user_id FK
Role "1" -- "0..*" RolePermission : role_permission.role_id FK
Permission "1" -- "0..*" RolePermission : role_permission.permission_id FK
Role "1" -- "0..*" UserRole : user_role.role_id FK
AppUser "1" ..> "0..*" UserRole : user_role.user_id\n(cross-context, no FK)
AppUser ..> Credentials : authenticate() consumes
AppUser --> AuthenticationType
UserSession --> SessionStatus

note right of Person
  RN-01/RN-02: a Person may exist without an
  active AppUser, but an AppUser cannot exist
  without a Person. RN-03: cannot be deleted
  with active records. No school_id — identity
  is school-agnostic.
end note

note right of AppUser
  RN-04/RN-06: must authenticate before use;
  admins may deactivate without deleting
  history. person_id is UNIQUE — one account
  per person.
end note

note right of UserSession
  sessionId is the opaque bearer token (never
  a JWT). refresh() rotates it: closes this row
  and returns a new UserSession — single use.
end note

note right of Role
  RN-07: roles are global, no school_id. Seeds:
  Administrador, Instructor, Aprendiz (legacy
  SUPER_ADMIN/SCHOOL_ADMIN/INSTRUCTOR/STUDENT
  merged).
end note

note right of Permission
  Format context.resource:action, e.g.
  attendance.justification:approve.
  RN-09/RN-10: access depends on the assigned
  role's permissions.
end note

note bottom of UserRole
  PK (user_id, role_id). RN-07: every AppUser
  must have at least one role.
end note

note as N1
  All classes also carry the standard audit block
  (created_at/updated_at/deleted_at/created_by/
  updated_by/deleted_by/row_version) — omitted
  here for readability. See AGENTS.md §2.2 and
  06-data/domains/01-identity.md /
  02-authorization.md for the column-level ER view.
end note

@enduml
